**Read:** [Industrial Chemical Technology II — Nduka, NOUN](../sources/Industrial-Chemical-Technology-II-NOUN.lingua#r_7RXE2GF1DW7QH9GHTCGT0P09SR), the complete synthesis-gas and oxo-process units; [Chemical Technology: From Principles to Products — Jess and Wasserscheid](../sources/Chemical-Technology-Jess-Wasserscheid.lingua#r_38DBBMW0BMR89K3R95V073YA41), the whole hydroformylation and acetic-acid industrial examples if chosen; [Organic Chemical Technology — Nanda Kishore, NPTEL](../sources/Organic-Chemical-Technology-Kishore.lingua#r_1ERYESBGNKCKMDY0NPHJKCVJG0), the complete relevant carbonyl-containing intermediate manufacturing sequence.

Carbonylation and hydroformylation add carbon monoxide into useful molecular frameworks through defined catalytic pathways. Hydroformylation also uses hydrogen to form aldehyde products from an alkene; the resulting positional/structural distribution matters to downstream use. A balanced carbon account does not by itself determine selectivity or catalyst performance.

Track catalyst form, ligands or other promoters, gas/liquid contact, phase behavior and possible deactivation. A rate measured in one solvent or composition region can change when transport or catalyst speciation changes. Reagent recycling, catalyst retention and impurity accumulation join the reaction with isolation.

For an acid or aldehyde product, identify the complete downstream separation and any further reaction. Gas recovery, solvent/catalyst loss, corrosion/contact materials and residual handling influence accepted output. A process may depend on proprietary preparation or operating details that the public account does not establish.

**Work:** reconstruct one complete authorized carbonylation/hydroformylation route and a justified alternative. Derive carbon/hydrogen/oxygen and catalyst/carrier inventories, test selectivity and isolation assumptions and compare full utility/product boundaries. Explain which primary kinetic, phase, analytical or service-history observation would distinguish competing process explanations.

**Continue:** [Connect aromatic oxygenated products with intermediate chemistry and co-product accounts](Phenol-cumene-intermediates-and-co-product-quality.lingua#r_1HRR8N9RMAQ8D1AMEDKAEZE5JY).

